{% comment %}
    SITE SEARCH — the search pill with live results under it. For an HTML
    block on any page that should offer search (the 404 page; a search page).

    Block content:            {% include '~~/Assets/Lava/SiteSearch.lava' %}
    Enabled Lava Commands:    RockEntity, Sql

    As the visitor types, theme.js ([data-site-search]) fetches the results
    from a Rock Lava Application endpoint (searchEndpoint, below) and swaps
    them into the results area, then puts ?q=… in the address bar so a reload
    or a shared link shows the same search. With ?q= in the URL, this file
    renders those results itself (Assets/Lava/SiteSearchResults.lava), so the
    page also works without JavaScript for shared links.

    The pill is a div, not a <form>: Rock wraps every page in one ASP.NET form
    and forms can't nest. theme.js keeps Enter from posting Rock's form back.

    Styled by Styles/_search.scss.
{% endcomment %}
{%- assign searchEndpoint = '/api/v2/lava-app/1/site/search' -%}

{%- assign searchQuery = 'Global' | PageParameter:'q' | Default:'' | Trim -%}

<div class="site-search">
  <div class="site-search__pill" data-site-search data-endpoint="{{ searchEndpoint }}" data-results="site-search-results" role="search">
    <label class="u-visually-hidden" for="site-search-q">Search the site</label>
    <input type="search" name="q" id="site-search-q" value="{{ searchQuery | Escape }}" placeholder="Search vrl.church…" autocomplete="off" enterkeyhint="search" />
    <button type="button" class="site-search__go" data-site-search-go aria-label="Search">
      <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8"/><path d="m21 21-4.3-4.3"/></svg>
    </button>
  </div>

  <div class="site-search__results" id="site-search-results" aria-live="polite">
    {%- if searchQuery != '' %}
    {% include '~~/Assets/Lava/SiteSearchResults.lava' %}
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</div>
